===Etymology===
{| class="floatright"
| {{PIE word|en|h₁én}}
| {{PIE word|en|h₂epó}}
|}{{root|en|ine-pro|*tḱey-}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from Late {{inh|en|enm|imposen|t=to place, set; to impose (a duty, etc.)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=impōsen|pos=v|id=MED22221}}</ref> borrowed from {{der|en|frm|imposer}}, and {{der|en|fro|emposer}}, {{m|fro|enposer|t=to impose (a duty, tax, etc.)}} (modern {{cog|fr|imposer}}), from {{m|fro|im-}}, {{m|fro|em-}} (variants of {{m|fro|en-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘in, into’}}) + {{m|fro|poser|t=to place, put}}, modelled after:<ref>{{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

* {{der|en|la|impōnō|impōnere|t=to place or set (something) on; (''figurative'') to impose (a duty, tax, etc.)}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=6026386821|date=December 2023}}</ref> from {{m|la|im-}} (variant of {{m|la|in-|pos=prefix meaning ‘on, upon’}}) + {{m|la|pōnō|t=to place, put; etc.}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂pó}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₂epó|t=away; off}} + {{m|ine-pro|*tḱey-|t=to cultivate; to live; to settle}}); and
* {{der|en|la|impositus|t=established; put upon, imposed}}, the {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|impōnō}}: see above.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the verb.<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=† impose|pos=n|id=1089664990|date=September 2023}}</ref>

